   "name": "bland-small-meals.md",
   "text": "title: Small, frequent bland meals\naka: BRAT diet, bland diet\ntags: health remedy\nwarn: The BRAT diet (bananas, rice, applesauce, toast) was historically promoted but MedlinePlus notes there is not strong evidence it is better than a standard bland diet; it probably does not cause harm. If nausea or vomiting persists beyond 24–48 hours, is accompanied by severe pain, or prevents adequate fluid intake, seek medical care.\nsource: https://medlineplus.gov/nauseaandvomiting.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#bland-small-meals\n\nEating 6–8 small bland meals throughout the day (crackers, toast, baked chicken, rice, potatoes) instead of 3 large meals reduces nausea and eases indigestion. As diarrhea symptoms improve, soft bland foods can be introduced gradually.\n\n## how\nEat smaller meals more often and stick to bland foods, avoiding spicy, fatty, or salty options. If you have trouble keeping food down, start with small sips of clear liquids frequently and add bland solids only when tolerated.\n\n## evidence\nMedlinePlus (NLM) recommends small, frequent bland meals and avoiding spicy, fatty, or salty foods as the primary dietary self-care for nausea and vomiting. For indigestion, MedlinePlus notes that avoiding foods and situations that trigger symptoms is the main home strategy. For diarrhea, 'soft, bland food' is recommended as symptoms improve.\n\n## safety\nThe BRAT diet (bananas, rice, applesauce, toast) was historically promoted but MedlinePlus notes there is not strong evidence it is better than a standard bland diet; it probably does not cause harm. If nausea or vomiting persists beyond 24–48 hours, is accompanied by severe pain, or prevents adequate fluid intake, seek medical care.\n\n## used for\n- Nausea & vomiting\n- Indigestion & upset stomach\n- Diarrhea\n\n## also said\n- feeling sick to my stomach, what can i eat\n- nauseous all day\n- what to eat after throwing up\n- upset stomach, what food\n- food after a stomach bug\n- BRAT diet does it work\n- bananas rice applesauce toast\n- what to eat with diarrhea\n- queasy and cant eat much\n- indigestion after big meals\n- stomach feels bad after eating\n- kid stopped vomiting, when can he eat\n- bland food list\n- how to start eating again after vomiting\n- nausea for 2 days, when to worry\n- crackers for nausea?\n- elderly mother nauseous and not eating\n- stomach upset, avoid what foods\n- morning sickness what to eat\n- small meals or big meals for nausea\n- i feel like vomit, what i eat\n- diarrhea getting better, what can i eat now\n"
