   "name": "carbon-monoxide.md",
   "text": "title: Carbon monoxide\naka: carbon monoxide, co poisoning, fumes, stove, stove indoors, heating indoors, charcoal indoors, dizzy, headache\ntags: fire shelter danger\nwarn: Never burn a fire, charcoal, gas stove, camping stove or generator inside a tent, car, closed shelter or room without proper ventilation. Carbon monoxide has no smell and kills in your sleep.\nsee: fire, shelter\nsource: compiled from general safety references, verify before relying on it\n\nCarbon monoxide is an invisible, odourless gas from anything that burns. In a closed space it builds up quickly.\n\n## symptoms\nHeadache, dizziness, weakness, nausea, confusion, sleepiness. Several people feeling ill at once in the same space is a strong sign.\n\n## how\nIf you suspect it: get everyone into fresh air immediately, open everything, and turn off or put out the source. Seek medical help. Do not go back in until the space is aired out.\n\n## safety\nCook and keep fires outside or under an open roof. Never bring a grill or charcoal inside to keep warm, even after the flames have gone out.\n\n## also said\n- co poisoning\n- carbon monoxide\n- fumes in the tent\n- everyone has a headache since we lit the stove\n- we all feel dizzy and sick in the cabin, the heater is on\n- can I bring the charcoal grill inside to keep warm, the flames are out\n- running the generator in the garage is that ok\n- camping stove inside the tent because its raining\n- my kids are very sleepy and confused after we used the gas heater indoors\n- grandpa says headache and nausea since we closed the windows with the fire going\n- is it safe to sleep in the car with the engine running for heat\n- what gas has no smell and kills you when you sleep\n- the embers in the bucket will keep the room warm right\n- how do I know if it's carbon monoxide or just flu\n- my wife and I both feel weak and want to throw up in the shelter\n- what to do if someone is poisoned by smoke fumes from a stove\n- cooking indoors on a camp stove is dangerous?\n- headache every morning in the hut we heat with the burner\n- can i use bbq inside the house when power is out\n- whole family dizzy, should we go outside\n- fresh air first or call doctor first\n- how long before we can go back inside after fumes\n- i cant smell anything so it must be safe?\n- heating a closed room with a charcoal pot\n- small tent heater ok overnight?\n- nausea confusion sleepy all at same time in same room\n- the dog and everyone else is sick in the camper\n- portable gas heater in the bedroom\n- is it ok to cook under a tarp roof\n- my head is pounding and I feel drunk but I didnt drink, stove is on\n- invisible gas from fire\n- someone passed out near the generator\n- open fire in a closed room no chimney danger\n- woke up groggy with headache after using the stove in the van\n- carbon monixide symptom\n- why is it dangerous to burn charcoal indoors even with no smoke\n"
