   "name": "echinacea.md",
   "text": "title: Echinacea\naka: Echinacea purpurea, purple coneflower\ntags: plant medicinal herb\nwarn: E. purpurea extracts appear likely safe for short periods in adults; allergic reactions can occur, with digestive symptoms most common. Children may experience rashes potentially linked to allergic reactions. Theoretical interactions with immunosuppressants and certain other drugs; consult a healthcare provider before use with medications. Limited data on safety in early pregnancy.\nsource: https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/echinacea, as summarised by Project NOMAD (natural_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/natural_remedies.json#echinacea\n\nEchinacea is primarily marketed for the common cold and upper respiratory tract infections, based on the idea that it may support immune system function.\n\n## evidence\nStudies indicate that taking echinacea may slightly reduce the chances of catching a cold, though evidence regarding whether it shortens cold duration is inconclusive. Evidence for other conditions, including eczema, is unclear.\n\n## safety\nE. purpurea extracts appear likely safe for short periods in adults; allergic reactions can occur, with digestive symptoms most common. Children may experience rashes potentially linked to allergic reactions. Theoretical interactions with immunosuppressants and certain other drugs; consult a healthcare provider before use with medications. Limited data on safety in early pregnancy.\n\n## used for\n- Common cold\n\n## also said\n- stop me catching a cold this winter\n- purple coneflower for colds\n- something to boost the immune system before cold season\n- does echinacea shorten a cold\n- will echinacea stop me getting sick\n- cone flower tea immune\n- echinacia safe for kids\n- my son got a rash after echinacea drops\n- echinacea with immunosuppressants after transplant\n- echinacea in early pregnancy\n- can i take echinacea for eczema\n- upper respiratory infection herbal prevention\n- how long is it safe to take echinacea\n- everyone at work is sick, how do i not catch it\n- purple daisy remedy for colds does it really work\n- immune herb that might lower chance of cold\n- echinacea upset stomach\n- e purpurea extract dosage\n- allergic reaction to coneflower\n- keep getting colds every month natural prevention\n- echinacea and methotrexate\n"
