   "name": "heating-pad.md",
   "text": "title: Heating pad or warm compress\ntags: health remedy\nwarn: Never fall asleep with a heating pad on — burns can result. For ear pain, do not insert anything into the ear canal; if pain is severe, accompanied by drainage, hearing loss, or fever, see a healthcare provider to rule out infection requiring antibiotics.\nsource: https://medlineplus.gov/periodpain.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#heating-pad\n\nApplying a heating pad or hot water bottle to the lower abdomen eases menstrual cramps. A warm compress applied to the ear can relieve earache discomfort. Heat may also be used on strained muscles after the first 48–72 hours of an acute injury.\n\n## how\nPlace a heating pad or hot water bottle on the lower abdomen for menstrual cramps, or hold a warm cloth against the affected ear for earache. Use a low or medium heat setting and put a cloth between the pad and skin to prevent burns.\n\n## evidence\nMedlinePlus (NIH/NLM) lists using a heating pad or hot water bottle on the lower abdomen, along with taking a warm bath, as home care measures for period pain. For earache, placing a warm cloth on the affected ear is listed among comfort measures in NIH/NLM resources for acute ear infection self-care.\n\n## safety\nNever fall asleep with a heating pad on — burns can result. Use a low or medium setting and place a cloth between the pad and skin. For ear pain, do not insert anything into the ear canal; if pain is severe, accompanied by drainage, hearing loss, or fever, see a healthcare provider to rule out infection requiring antibiotics.\n\n## used for\n- Menstrual cramps\n- Muscle & joint pain\n- Earache & ear wax\n\n## also said\n- bad period cramps\n- period pain and no painkillers\n- cramps in lower belly from my period\n- my daughter has her first period and cramps\n- earache, what can i do at home\n- kid says his ear hurts\n- ear pain at night, no doctor\n- hot water bottle for cramps\n- how to use a heating pad safely\n- can i sleep with a heating pad\n- warm cloth on ear for earache\n- muscle still stiff a week after injury, heat now?\n- when can i switch from ice to heat\n- sore back muscles a few days after straining it\n- menstrual pain relief without pills\n- ear hurting and leaking something\n- grandpa has ear pain, how to soothe\n- stomach cramps during my period, what helps\n- ache in my ear after swimming\n- old pulled muscle still sore, warm it?\n- period hurting so much i cant stand\n- pain in ear for baby, what to do\n"
