   "name": "ice-and-elevation.md",
   "text": "title: Ice and elevation (RICE method)\naka: RICE, Rest-Ice-Compression-Elevation\ntags: health remedy\nwarn: Never apply ice directly to skin — always wrap it in a cloth or towel. If swelling worsens significantly, numbness develops, or you suspect a fracture, seek medical evaluation. Do not use heat during the first 48–72 hours of an acute soft-tissue injury.\nsource: https://medlineplus.gov/sprainsandstrains.html, as summarised by Project NOMAD (home_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/home_remedies.json#ice-and-elevation\n\nApplying ice wrapped in cloth to a strained muscle, sprain, or bite site — combined with rest, compression, and elevation of the injured area — reduces swelling and pain. Ice should be applied for 10–15 minutes every 1–3 hours during the first few days of injury.\n\n## how\nWrap ice in a cloth or towel and apply to the injured area for 10–15 minutes at a time. Rest the area, wrap it snugly with a bandage to reduce swelling, and elevate it above heart level when possible.\n\n## evidence\nMedlinePlus (NIH/NIAMS) describes the RICE method as standard first-line treatment for sprains and strains: resting the area, icing it, compressing it with a bandage, and elevating it above heart level when possible. Ice use for the first 3 days is specifically mentioned.\n\n## safety\nNever apply ice directly to skin — always wrap it in a cloth or towel. If swelling worsens significantly, numbness develops, or you suspect a fracture, seek medical evaluation. Do not use heat during the first 48–72 hours of an acute soft-tissue injury.\n\n## used for\n- Muscle & joint pain\n- Insect bites & stings\n\n## also said\n- twisted my ankle on the hike\n- sprained my wrist, it's swelling\n- rolled my ankle and its puffy\n- pulled a muscle in my leg\n- knee swollen after falling\n- how to treat a sprain\n- what is RICE\n- should i use ice or heat on a new injury\n- how long do i keep ice on a sprain\n- hurt my back lifting, just happened\n- swollen ankle after a fall, cant see a doctor\n- how to wrap a sprained ankle\n- why raise the leg above the heart\n- ankle turned on rocks, far from help, can walk a bit\n- kid fell off bike, wrist swollen\n- grandma tripped and her knee is swelling\n- strained my calf running\n- injury swelling up fast what do i do\n- is it broken or sprained how do i know\n- my foot is swollen and numb after twisting it\n- jammed finger swollen\n- twist my foot, very painful, how to make swelling go down\n"
