   "name": "nettle.md",
   "text": "title: Stinging nettle\naka: nettle, nettles, urtica, urtica dioica, ortie\ntags: plant wild food fibre\nwarn: Wear gloves to pick. Do not eat raw unless crushed or dried. Never pick from roadsides or sprayed fields.\nsee: foraging-rules\nsource: compiled from general foraging references, verify before relying on it\n\nA common, very nutritious wild green that grows near people, paths and rich soil. One of the safest plants to learn first because its sting makes it hard to confuse.\n\n## identify\nUpright stems up to about 1.5 m, square in section. Leaves in opposite pairs, heart-shaped to pointed, with toothed edges. The whole plant is covered in fine stinging hairs. Small greenish flowers hang in strings in summer.\n\n## harvest\nPick the top four to six young leaves in spring, before the plant flowers. Older plants are tough and less pleasant. Cutting plants back makes them regrow fresh tops later in the season.\n\n## eat\nCooking, blanching or drying removes the sting completely. Use like spinach: soup, stew, with eggs or potatoes. Dried leaves make tea.\n\n## use\nStem fibres can be made into string and cord. Nettles make a strong liquid fertiliser when soaked in water for two to three weeks.\n\n## also said\n- nettle\n- nettles\n- stinging nettle soup\n- ortie\n- plant that stings when you touch it can you eat it\n- how to pick nettles without getting stung\n- does cooking take away the sting\n- can i eat nettles raw\n- nettle tea\n- dried nettle leaves\n- which part of the nettle should I pick\n- nettle tops in spring\n- nettles flowering, still good to eat?\n- old nettles tough and stringy\n- cut back nettles to get new growth\n- nettle like spinach recipe\n- can i make rope from nettles\n- string from plant fibres\n- cordage from nettle stems\n- nettle fertiliser for garden\n- liquid plant food from soaking weeds\n- square stem with hairs that burn, what is it\n- leaves in pairs with toothed edges and stinging hairs\n- nettles growing by the path can we use them\n- is nettle safe for kids to eat\n- green strings of tiny flowers hanging on the stinging plant\n- nutritious wild green that is easy to identify\n- safest wild plant for a beginner\n- urtica dioica edible\n- nettles with eggs or potatoes\n- how long to soak nettles for fertilizer\n- blanch nettles how\n- i got stung picking the nettles do i need gloves\n- can i crush nettle leaves and eat them\n- nettle near roadside ok to eat?\n- the weed that burns my legs in the garden is it food\n"
