   "name": "passionflower.md",
   "text": "title: Passionflower\naka: Passiflora incarnata\ntags: plant medicinal herb\nwarn: Taking passionflower alongside anesthesia or other surgical medications may slow the nervous system too much; avoid use before surgery. Should not be used during pregnancy as it may induce uterine contractions.\nsource: https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/passionflower, as summarised by Project NOMAD (natural_remedies.json, commit 54ee30a)\nlicence: text Apache-2.0 (Project NOMAD), summarising a US government page (public domain)\norigin: nomad/natural_remedies.json#passionflower\n\nPassionflower is marketed as a dietary supplement for anxiety, sleep problems, and stress.\n\n## how\nPassionflower is taken as a tea (studied for up to 7 nights) or as an oral extract supplement (studied for up to 8 weeks). Follow package directions and consult a healthcare provider before use, especially if you take other medications or are scheduled for surgery.\n\n## evidence\nSome research suggests oral passionflower may help reduce anxiety symptoms and improve total sleep time in adults with insomnia, though findings on falling or staying asleep are mixed and conclusions are not definite.\n\n## safety\nTaking passionflower alongside anesthesia or other surgical medications may slow the nervous system too much; avoid use before surgery. Should not be used during pregnancy as it may induce uterine contractions. Possible side effects include drowsiness, dizziness, and confusion. Discuss with a healthcare provider before combining with medications.\n\n## used for\n- Sleeplessness\n\n## also said\n- passion flower tea for sleep\n- passionflower before surgery\n- having an operation, stop calming herbs?\n- passionflower and anesthesia\n- passionflower in pregnancy\n- calming herb that can cause contractions\n- passiflora for anxiety\n- maypop for nerves\n- passionflower extract 8 weeks\n- passion flower made me confused and dizzy\n- herb tea to sleep longer, insomnia\n- total sleep time herbal tea\n- passionflower with antidepressants\n- pasion flower for stress\n- vine flower supplement for anxiety does it work\n- how many nights of passionflower tea\n- passionflower drowsy next day\n- passionflower and sleeping pills\n- anxious before a test, passionflower ok\n- passiflora incarnata dosage\n"
