   "name": "wild-garlic.md",
   "text": "title: Wild garlic\naka: wild garlic, ramsons, ramson, bear garlic, baerlauch, allium ursinum, ail des ours\ntags: plant wild food\nwarn: Deadly lookalikes. Lily of the valley and autumn crocus grow in the same places and have similar leaves. Three or four autumn crocus leaves can kill. If in doubt, do not eat it.\nsee: deadly-lookalikes, foraging-rules\nsource: German Federal Institute for Risk Assessment (BfR) press releases on wild garlic; Austrian food safety agency (AGES)\n\nA spring woodland plant with a strong garlic smell. Delicious, but every year people are poisoned, sometimes fatally, by confusing it with toxic plants.\n\n## identify\n- Each leaf grows on its own thin stalk straight out of the ground.\n- Leaves are soft, bright green, matt underneath, with one clear central vein.\n- A crushed leaf smells strongly of garlic.\n- White star-shaped flowers in round clusters, from about May.\n- Found in damp, shady deciduous woods and along streams, from about March to May.\n\nLily of the valley: usually two leaves wrapped around one stem, firm, shiny underneath, no garlic smell.\nAutumn crocus: several leaves grow together from one point, rubbery, no garlic smell. Flowers only in autumn.\n\n## safety\nThe smell test is unreliable once your hands already smell of garlic from earlier leaves. Check every single leaf, one by one. Never pull up handfuls. Wash wild leaves well.\n\n## eat\nRaw in salads, as pesto, in soups and with eggs or potatoes. Best before flowering.\n\n## also said\n- wild garlic\n- ramsons\n- baerlauch\n- bear garlic\n- leaves in the forest smell like garlic can i eat them\n- wild garlic or lily of the valley\n- wild garlic or autumn crocus how to tell\n- found a carpet of green leaves in the woods by the stream in april\n- how to identify wild garlic safely\n- my hands smell of garlic now I cant tell which leaves\n- does the smell test work for wild garlic\n- wild garlic pesto\n- when is wild garlic season\n- white star flowers in round balls in the woods\n- each leaf has its own stem, is it ramsons\n- leaves shiny underneath, still wild garlic?\n- several leaves growing from one point, is it garlic\n- people died from wild garlic lookalike?\n- ail des ours\n- can I eat wild garlic raw\n- wild garlic after flowering still good?\n- picked a bag of baerlauch, one leaf doesnt smell\n- check each leaf of wild garlic\n- allium ursinum\n- broad soft leaves in shady wood garlic smell\n- is it bad to pull handfuls of wild garlic\n- wild garlic soup\n- wild garlic with eggs\n- foraging ramps in germany\n- leaves look like wild garlic but no smell\n- wash wild garlic leaves?\n- my wife picked garlic leaves in the forest, how sure can we be\n- where does wild garlic grow\n- garlic leaves from the woods, what poisonous plant looks the same\n- matt underneath with one middle vein, garlic?\n- kids picked garlicky leaves on the walk, safe?\n- the garlic leaves were near lily of valley flowers\n"
